==Spanish==
{{number box|es}}

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably partly borrowed from {{der|es|la|medius}} as a semi-learned form or modified from an existing inherited early {{cog|osp|-}} equivalent, presumably {{m|osp||*meo}} or {{m|osp||*meyo}}, to be closer to the Latin origin (possibly in order to avoid a phonetic similarity with the vulgar verb {{m|es|mear|t=to piss}}).<ref>{{R:es:DCECH}}</ref><ref>{{R:es:DCECH}}</ref> Compare {{cog|pt|meio}}, which retained its original inherited form. The sense of "medium" is taken from {{cog|la|medium}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|medium}}.

====Adjective====
{{es-adj}}

# [[half]], {{ngd|of or related to one of two equal divisions of a whole}}
#: {{uxi|es|'''media''' hora|'''half''' hour}}
#: {{uxi|es|'''media''' manzana|'''half''' an apple}}
# {{lb|es|inexact}} [[half]], {{ngd|of or related to any large proportion of a whole}}
#: {{uxi|es|'''Medio''' Nueva York fue a los toros.|'''Half''' of New York went to the bullfight.}}
# [[middle]], {{ngd|placed more or less halfway between two positions, times, or alternatives}}
#: {{uxi|es|clase '''media'''|'''middle''' class}}
# [[average]], {{ngd|of or related to the arithmatic middle in a set of values}}
#: {{uxi|es|velocidad '''media'''|'''average''' speed}}
# [[average]], {{ngd|of or related to a representative example of a group}}
#: {{ux|es|el español '''medio'''|the '''average''' Spaniard... your '''typical''' Spaniard...}}
# {{lb|es|art}} [[tasteful]], [[bourgeois]], {{ngd|well decorated or executed but not sublime}}
# {{lb|es|linguistics}} [[mid]], {{ngd|of or related to the position of vowel articulation between open and closed}}
# {{lb|es|grammar}} [[middle]], [[mediopassive]], {{ngd|of or related to grammatical voices neither active nor passive}}
# {{lb|es|Chile|slang|ironic|intensifier}} [[impressive]], {{ngd|extremely large or good}}
#: {{uxi|es|¡'''Media''' bolsa!|'''Such a huge''' bag! '''What an awesome''' bag! '''Whatta''' bag!}}

